            <div class="step5-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Strengths</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/mandala-2.png">
                <p><strong>They Really Do Have Good Intentions</strong></p>
                <p><strong>They Have Good Intentions</strong></p>
                <p>Outlaws don&rsquo;t always come across as the most cooperative or even warmest of people.However, they are hugely compassionate and are generally very nice people with kind intentions.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>However, the Outlaw&rsquo;s difficulties with expressing themselves and in finding a peaceful place to live freely (internally and externally) can cause them to appear angry, abrupt or inconsiderate of others.It wouldn&rsquo;t be exaggerating to say that an Outlaw will sacrifice all of themselves to liberate themselves and others.There are not too many other archetypes who would do that</p>
                <p><strong>Outlaws Are Compassionate</strong></p>
                <p>Most people don&rsquo;t stop to notice how compassionate an Outlaw is.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Ok, so they might not be too sympathetic about your injured knee, especially if they are focused on a project that will help more people.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>But they do care about nature and humanity in particular, and it&rsquo;s this compassion that usually drives them to do whatever it is they are working on rather than paying attention to your injury.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Trust us, they mean well.</p>
                <p><strong>Passionate in All That They Do</strong></p>
                <p>Outlaws are probably in the top range of archetypes who express incredible passion.It&rsquo;s this passion that drives them, but unfortunately, it also gets them into trouble.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>If they could learn to align this passion so that it's productive, they&rsquo;d have an easier time.We are just not sure that the Outlaw would have any intention of adjusting themselves unless it helps a greater cause!</p>
                <p><strong>Outlaws Have A Keen Eye for The Problems That Need Solving in The World</strong></p>
                <p>Outlaws usually know before most other people what problems need to be addressed in the world.They are often labeled &lsquo;troublemakers,&rsquo; &lsquo;conspiracy theorists,&rsquo; &lsquo;activists&rsquo; and so on which are all relatively demeaning because usually, the Outlaw is onto something for real.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It&rsquo;s just that the knowledge hasn&rsquo;t hit the mainstream just yet (or is being kept from the mainstream) and people have been trained not to take such activism seriously.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>If only people would stop to listen to an Outlaw and look at what they are trying to show them, then they&rsquo;d be at the cutting edge of what is happening in the world.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>We're confident that at least 80% of Outlaws are highlighting some truth.</p>
                
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Weaknesses</h2>
                <p><strong>Always Misunderstood</strong></p>
                <p>Outlaws can be their own worst enemy most of the time.They live in such conflict and chaos because of their fight for freedom, and they have so much passion that they can sometimes be forthright or even forceful in their opinions, ventures, or refusal to conform to reasonable expectations in society.This can lead them to be misunderstood by others as being difficult or destructive when they are usually just trying to stand up for what is right to them.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Outlaws Rebel Against Themselves</strong></p>
                <p>Because Outlaw&rsquo;s hate rules and restrictions with a passion, they can often challenge their own limitations and restrictions.As we&rsquo;ve already mentioned, we need some routine and regular cycles, and it&rsquo;s usual to be obligated to do something.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Sometimes the Outlaw can become frustrated with the very things that assist them in living a healthy and balanced life, just because they cannot stand rules, and obligations.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Extremely Cynical </strong></p>
                <p>While Outlaws often have an eye for noticing things that really should be addressed, they can become overly cynical too.Outlaw&rsquo;s don&rsquo;t find it easy to trust anyone or anything and will question everything.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>But because they are so passionate about freedom, they often to forget to apply critical thinking to everything, including assessing why they are so cynical and whether it&rsquo;s necessary.If Outlaw's were to do this, they might find that they have a different perspective on some things and therefore a different approach.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>Outlaws Have Difficulty in Expressing Themselves</strong></p>
                <p>This aspect of an Outlaw&rsquo;s personality has already been mentioned because it&rsquo;s such a huge challenge for them.It&rsquo;s one of their major weaknesses and is the byproduct of all of their thoughts, beliefs and experiences combined and can be addressed, if the Outlaw chooses to do so.They just need to practice patience and diligence as they consciously make an effort to learn how to express themselves in a way that gets them heard and understood.</p>
                <div class="prev-next">
                    <div class="container">
                        <div class="row mx-auto col-reverse">
                            <div class="col-sm-6 mx-auto">
                                <button class="btn step4-back hover f-left">4. Personality Traits</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="col-sm-6">
                                <button class="btn step6 hover f-right">6. Greatest Challenge</button>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step6-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?>'s Greatest Challenge</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/success.png">
                <p>The problem for an Outlaw is that even though they advocate change like no other archetype, it&rsquo;s not often the Outlaw who creates change in the world.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Sure, they might make some noise, and draw attention to things.But unless they can learn to deal with some of their issues over needing to discipline themselves to attain the freedom they seek, they won&rsquo;t get further than that.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Which means that the sense of significance and contribution that the Outlaw needs (yes, even Outlaws need a sense of significance and contribution) is undermined and can cause the Outlaw to feel unfulfilled in general.</p>
                <p>Which leads us to the Outlaw&rsquo;s greatest challenge&hellip;</p>
                <p>The Outlaw needs to become organized and disciplined in the way that they live their life, manage projects, organize their thoughts and pick their fights.If they do so, then they can make an incredible difference to the world.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It sounds easy, but to an Outlaw, this is particularly difficult because they hate to be tied down, hate having to conform, or sticking to rules - even their own - and this problem is usually profoundly ingrained in them.They can also find a lot of fights to pick, far too many for anybody to reasonably make a difference to.</p>
                <p>To change this pattern, an Outlaw will have to go against everything they stand for, which is why this challenge is particularly had for them- it is their greatest challenge after all.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>In doing so, they will gain everything and make an incredible difference as well as attaining a strong sense of significance and contribution to the world.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It&rsquo;s one of the hardest contradictions out of all of the archetypes!&nbsp;</p>
                <p>But if the Outlaw can understand that to create order out of chaos, there has to be some structure and where there&rsquo;s structure there usually is limitation, and then if they can consciously apply this principle to their life, they might master their greatest challenge.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Of course, the Outlaw will need to take time to think about this, and probably learn how to prioritize, organize their thoughts and focus of attention before they can get started on this challenge.But it&rsquo;s entirely possible to do in a way that doesn&rsquo;t cause the Outlaw to feel to restricted.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>It&rsquo;s usually archetypes such as the Magician, the Hero, the Creator, or the Ruler who manage to bring about the change the Outlaw desires.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>But if the Outlaw can master their greatest challenge, they will be at the top of the list of movers and shakers, which is where they should be for their efforts and compassionate intentions.&nbsp;</p>
                <p><strong>How the Outlaw archetype can master their greatest challenge</strong></p>
                <p>To overcome their greatest challenge the Outlaw needs to keep an open mind and look at how they live their life so that they can determine what it&rsquo;s missing, what changes they&rsquo;d like to bring to the world and why they never seem to get very far in their efforts.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>If they can also take time to notice the limitations, they place on themselves by trying to be &lsquo;too free&rsquo; they can move their life in the direction of their dreams.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>The process of individuation is a wonderful tool that will significantly help the Outlaw to start to use their integrity and passion in all the right places and to permit themselves to take the actions that they need to take to bring in the sense of unconditional freedom that always seems to be out of reach for them.</p>
                <p>Shadow work, in particular, is an integral part of this process and you can learn more about this in the Premium Archetype Reports.</p>
                <div class="prev-next">
                    <div class="container">
                        <div class="row mx-auto col-reverse">
                            <div class="col-sm-6 mx-auto">
                                <button class="btn step5-back hover f-left">5. Strengths/Weaknesses</button>
                            </div>
                            <div class="col-sm-6">
                                <button class="btn step7 hover f-right">7. Conclusion</button>
                            </div>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="step7-reading">
                <h2 class="step-title"><?php echo $_GET['archetype'];?> Archetype - Conclusion</h2>
                <img class="img-intext" src="/offer/paa/img/joy.png">
                <p>Few archetypes will ever be as dedicated to their mission as the Outlaw archetype.</p>
                <p>However, even though the Outlaw seeks to pay attention to the things that need to change in the world, they are often not as innovative in their approach to solving the problems as they would like to be because they haven&rsquo;t found the balance between being free and creating change.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>They also haven&rsquo;t learned how to express themselves in a way that is congruent, and relatable.</p>
                <p>If the Outlaw was to find the balance between purposeful structure, (which is needed to attain a higher goal) versus forced structure, and even to develop a respect for the fair structures that we all need to stay out of chaos, the Outlaw really can do some great work and make a significant impact upon the world.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>What you have read so far is just an introduction and a tiny portion of what we can tell you about The Outlaw Archetype. It doesn&rsquo;t matter where you are as an Outlaw in your journey; whether you&rsquo;ve already heard your &lsquo;call to action&rsquo; and may have started to implement the changes, you must make to overcome your greatest challenge.Whether you&rsquo;ve already achieved a sense of &lsquo;contribution.&rsquo;Or whether you have found this report to be eye-opening from the offset.</p>
                <p>The thing is, we &lsquo;get you,&rsquo; we know your call to action or your greatest challenge, we know the lessons you have to learn and how you might respond to them, and if you felt as though we understood you, that was because we do.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>We know how to help you to uncover and reconcile the hidden aspects of your &lsquo;self&rsquo; so that when you do, all internal conflict fades away and what is left behind is a balanced, whole and strong individual who can navigate life on their terms while connecting with the right people deeply.</p>
                <p>We have spent years understanding the Outlaw Archetype, and have built on and adapted Jung&rsquo;s work to ensure that you achieve great success in your quest for liberation.</p>
                <p>We continue to learn more about you and update our content as you send in your life stories and experiences.</p>
                <p>Slowly and surely, we have understood how the Outlaw thinks, relates and connects.Why they do what they do and what they need to discover to reach their full potential.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>This is how we know that many of the challenges you&rsquo;ve faced and will face in the future have been and can be reconciled, even if you cannot see how at this moment in time.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>But to reconcile your &lsquo;self,&rsquo; YOU need to understand more about yourself. You need to discover your little (and big) traits so that you can understand them, accept them and work with them, or change them (if they do not serve you).&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Life is fleeting, and you don&rsquo;t have to live your life in conflict and disruption because of your disdain for freedom. You don&rsquo;t have to stand by, and watch others make the changes to the world that you are so capable of doing.You can make changes in the world, and you can learn to bring about change without feeling trapped by limitation. You just need to learn how.</p>
                <p>To learn how, you need to go much deeper into your psyche, and start to uncover the secrets that you keep even from yourself, you need to learn about the secret lives of your unexpressed world and understand how your underworld can cause conflict in your reality - and then you need to learn how to reconcile it.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Once you&rsquo;ve learned about your hidden self, you need to protect your newly found sense of wholeness.You can do this by learning how hidden forces influenced by timing, affect different phases of your life, forces that are seeking to achieve wholeness and are prompting you to reconcile parts of yourself so that you can feel complete; this is all part of the process of individuation.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>Most people don&rsquo;t realize that these forces exist and then when they walk into problems in later life they are completely mystified as to how the new challenges they face came about!&nbsp;</p>
                <p>If you can develop an awareness of these factors and build strategies into your life by reconciling them as part of the individuation process, you will be able to conquer your shadows before them conquering you.&nbsp;</p>
                <p>The Premium Archetype Reports teach you how to develop an awareness of the depths of your soul, and it's needs, and then it presents you with coping strategies and resources to help you satisfy your deepest desires so that you feel utterly fulfilled.</p>
                <p>Are you ready to learn what really drives you as a Ruler? What secretly motivates and inspires you? And what you are afraid of?</p>
